  "term": "exorcism",
  "definition": "Exorcism is the practice of trying to drive evil spirits out of a person or place by spoken formulas or prescribed rites. In the historical view given here, it rests on the belief that illness or misfortune is caused by a spirit and can be removed by expelling or sometimes appeasing it.",
